<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["ProjectHub.Web.styles.css"]" />

    <!-- MudBlazor requires the Roboto font and its bundled CSS. These replace Bootstrap entirely; we keep only
         app.css for our own overrides. Loading them here (not per-page) means the theme is available before the
         first component renders, avoiding a flash of unstyled content. -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Roboto:300,400,500,700&display=swap" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/MudBlazor/MudBlazor.min.css" />

    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="@(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))" />
</head>

<body>
    <!--
        THE BOOT SPLASH — static HTML, not a component.

        <Routes> below renders with prerender:false, which means the server sends a body containing nothing but a
        Blazor placeholder comment. The browser therefore has NOTHING to paint until the SignalR circuit connects
        and the first render arrives: a blank white page for the whole of that window, which on a cold start or a
        slow connection reads as an app that has failed to load.

        This markup is plain HTML with inlined styles so it paints on the very first byte, before app.css or
        MudBlazor's stylesheet have necessarily arrived. AuthenticationGate removes it (via projectHubBoot.hideSplash)
        once the app has something of its own to show. It must be removed from JS rather than by Blazor because it
        lives outside the component tree, so Blazor never owns it.
    -->
    <div id="ph-splash" class="ph-boot">
        <div class="ph-boot-brand">ProjectHub</div>
        <div class="ph-boot-spinner" role="status" aria-label="Loading ProjectHub"></div>
        <noscript>
            <p style="font: 500 14px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; color: #64748b; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                ProjectHub needs JavaScript to run. Please enable it and reload.
            </p>
        </noscript>
    </div>

    <Routes @rendermode="@(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))" />

    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
    <!-- MudBlazor's JS powers ripples, popovers, dialogs, and the snackbar. It must load after blazor.web.js so
         its interop hooks attach to an initialized runtime. -->
    <script src="_content/MudBlazor/MudBlazor.min.js"></script>
    <!-- Our own helpers, loaded last so their globals exist before any component invokes them.
         fileDownload: turns attachment bytes into a Blob download — see the file for why the bytes are
         round-tripped through C# instead of exposing a naked API URL.
         boot: removes the splash above once the app is live. -->
    <script src="js/fileDownload.js"></script>
    <script src="js/boot.js"></script>
</body>

</html>
